WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.301
Week 34: Pan-Hispanic Variation and Dialect Listening. recognize major regional forms ask for clarification without judgment adapt address and vocabulary

2
00:00:11.301 --> 00:00:21.153
Cultural lens. Spain, Mexico, the Caribbean, Central America, the Andes, the River Plate, and U.S. Spanish are internally diverse.

3
00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:33.225
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:33.225 --> 00:00:45.083
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:54.082
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:54.082 --> 00:01:29.769
Model language. España, México y el Caribe no hablan igual. — Spain, Mexico, and the Caribbean don't speak the same way. Los Andes y el Río de la Plata también son distintos. — The Andes and the River Plate are also different. Cada país hispanohablante es internamente diverso. — Every Spanish-speaking country is internally diverse. Ningún país representa la totalidad del español. — No country represents the whole of Spanish. Es mejor evitar la caricatura de un acento. — It's best to avoid caricaturing an accent.

7
00:01:29.769 --> 00:01:39.689
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
